comments:
Pymodbus API changed in 3.8 where the `values` parameter of `write_registers` must be a list.

In pymodbus 3.7 and earlier the values could be a list or a single int, so code that passes a single int to pymodbus write function will break in pymodbus 3.8

@SNCWilkinson I've updated solaredge-modbus-multi to address this since I was passing single values for write commands.
